speechtext:
This will not take long. Out of 630,000 farms across Canada we find that
423,000	have no water supply piped into the

house; 528,000 have no bathrooms or showers;
473.000	have neither flush nor chemical toilets; 275,000 have no electricity for lighting;
535.000	still use wood or coal for cooking and 427,000 have no refrigeration.
These figures show that 51-5 per cent have electricity, 17-5 per cent have hot and cold running water, 15 [DOT] 5 per cent have bathing and shower facilities and 21-9 per cent have refrigeration. I will let the people of Canada be the judge of whether the minister is correct in his statement that the farmers are better off than they ever were before.
